# Extra environment for checks/72-egress-enforce.sh: the egress firewall at its DEFAULT.
# smoke.env turns the firewall off for the other checks. An empty value is "unset", and unset is
# ON, so this line puts the default back (a later env file wins over an earlier one).
EGRESS_ENFORCE=
# The one network the workload may reach directly: the fake upstream of this instance (the check
# starts it at 172.30.86.10), which lets the check prove that the allowlist opens exactly that.
EGRESS_ALLOW_CIDRS=172.30.86.10/32
